[Music]  right now america is facing a labor  crisis and  i don't mean the kind where a woman  gives birth in a taxi i mean the kind  where millions of people are out of a  job  at one point during the pandemic the  unemployment rate was at its highest  level  since the great depression but as  america begins to open back  up it turns out not everyone is open to  going back to work  because a lot of people are making more  money on unemployment  than they did at their previous jobs  like a lot  a lot according to one study two-thirds  of jobless workers would make more money  from unemployment  plus the federal government supplement  than they would have on the job  which explains why many americans are  reluctant to return to work  now the media keeps referring to this  situation as a quote  worker shortage but america doesn't have  a worker shortage  we have a shortage of workers willing to  take a job unless they receive a living  wage  our current national minimum wage is  7.25 an hour  that's not a living wage in 2021 and  that wasn't a living wage in 1971  and back then the only things you needed  to pay for were rent electricity  and a pair of these you know it looks  good  pictures are popping up all over the  country of signs posted on businesses  saying they're closed or short-staffed  because quote  no one wants to work anymore happy face  which  by the way is a truly passive aggressive  use of a smiley face  the only worst use would be this  well let me set the record straight all  my life i've heard the same argument  if you don't want to earn minimum wage  get a better job well guess what  that's what people are doing they're  waiting to find a job that respects them  and pays them it turns out the free  market also means that workers are free  to only work at the job is worth it  not just because the job is there can  you imagine going on a date every time  someone asked you just because they  asked and when you asked what you were  going to do on the date they said  make you work until you're 65 but you're  still going to die poor  that's a terrible date do not go out  with them  since the financial crisis of 2008  employers have become accustomed to  paying low wages  so that they can line the pockets of  high-level executives  and just like that other type of labor  crisis the people most affected are  women  during the pandemic countless women had  to leave their jobs to take care of  their children  do you know why because no one else was  going to do it  do you think they don't want to go back  to work i mean  have you ever met a child they will ask  you 273 questions in a row  and then sneeze in your mouth of course  those women want to go back to work  but they need a job that pays them  enough to do it  you can't ask a person to work a minimum  wage job at 7.25 an hour when they have  to pay  20 dollars an hour to get a babysitter  and before you ask  yes that's how much a good babysitter  costs do you think claudia kishi can  dress like this on a budget  until america catches up with much of  the rest of the developed world and  provides viable child care  women are pretty much screwed and not in  the fun way that help them make those  kids in the first place  so from now on don't get mad when you  see one of these signs  get excited people are literally pulling  themselves up by their bootstraps by  demanding to earn enough money to buy  some goddamn boots  and if you're in the middle of this  cluster right now  listen to me you are not lazy you  deserve to be able to work one job that  covers the basic necessities like food  shelter clothes and a subscription to  peacock  i'm just kidding peacock is actually  free you don't even need to enter a  credit card number to sign up just an  email address and a password so do it  but most importantly you deserve to work  in a safe environment with employers who  value your life  oh by the way if you're a business owner  who refuses to pay a living wage and  then complains when no one wants to work  for you  you are not a business owner you are a  plantation owner but your plantation  is a frozen yogurt shop listen we could  be living through one of the greatest  labor movements in history because  knowing your worth is revolutionary  and this is a revolution baby so go get  your money you  earned it  you

